@* Layout (UI docs). Sections: Usage, Examples, Customization, Styling reference, API, Accessibility, Guidelines. *@

<ul class="dnf-docs-source">
    <li>CSS <code>src/DotNetForge.UI/Styles/components/layout.css</code></li>
</ul>

<h2 id="usage">Usage</h2>
<p>A few layout primitives for the patterns every screen repeats: stack, cluster, spread, grid, split, container, divider,
    note and skip link. Anything else about placement is Tailwind utilities in the markup (<code>flex</code>,
    <code>gap-*</code>, <code>grid-cols-*</code>). The grey boxes below are placeholders.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="basic" layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-stack">
        <div class="dnf-spread">
            <strong>Recent pages</strong>
            <dnf-button size="Sm">View all</dnf-button>
        </div>
        <div class="dnf-grid dnf-grid--cols-3">
            <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">Home</div>
            <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">About us</div>
            <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">Contact</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<h2 id="examples">Examples</h2>

<ui-doc-example id="stack" title="Stack" description="Children in a column with one gap: dnf-stack (space-4), --sm (space-2) and --lg (space-6)." layout="block">
