<h2 id="customization">Customization</h2>
<p>The three <a href="@UiDocsCatalog.Root/customization">customization levels</a>, none needing <code>!important</code>.</p>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-tailwind" title="Tailwind utilities" description="A utility beats the component's own value - here a gap-1 stack and a gap-8 cluster." layout="stack">
    <div class="dnf-stack gap-1">
        <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">gap-1</div>
        <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">gap-1</div>
    </div>
    <div class="dnf-cluster gap-8">
        <dnf-badge>gap-8</dnf-badge>
        <dnf-badge>gap-8</dnf-badge>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-example id="custom-css" title="Your own CSS" description="Unlayered CSS changes a primitive in a scope - here a five-column grid." layout="block">
    <div class="dnf-docs-demo-grid">
        <div class="dnf-grid">
            <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">1</div>
            <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">2</div>
            <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">3</div>
            <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">4</div>
            <div class="rounded-md border border-border bg-surface-muted p-3 text-sm">5</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</ui-doc-example>

<ui-doc-code id="custom-css-code" lang="css">
.dnf-docs-demo-grid .dnf-grid {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(5, minmax(0, 1fr));
}
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="styling">Styling reference</h2>
<h3 id="classes">Classes</h3>
<table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Kind</th><th>Effect</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-stack</code></td><td>block</td><td>a flex column, gap <code>--dnf-space-4</code>, <code>min-width: 0</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-stack--sm</code> / <code>--lg</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>gap <code>--dnf-space-2</code> / <code>--dnf-space-6</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-cluster</code></td><td>block</td><td>a wrapping, vertically centred row, gap <code>--dnf-space-2</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-cluster--lg</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>gap <code>--dnf-space-4</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-spread</code></td><td>block</td><td>a centred row, <code>justify-content: space-between</code>, gap <code>--dnf-space-4</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-grid</code></td><td>block</td><td>a grid, gap <code>--dnf-space-5</code>; set the columns with a modifier</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-grid--cols-2</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>2 columns; 1 below 40rem</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-grid--cols-3</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>3 columns; 2 below 64rem; 1 below 40rem</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-grid--cols-4</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>4 columns; 2 below 64rem (gap <code>--dnf-space-3</code> below 40rem)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-grid--auto</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>as many 16rem-minimum tracks as fit</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-split</code></td><td>block</td><td>main column + a 15-19rem side column; one column without <code>__aside</code>; stacks below 80rem</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-split__main</code>, <code>dnf-split__aside</code></td><td>element</td><td>columns of cards, gap <code>--dnf-space-5</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-split__aside</code></td><td>element</td><td>sticky below the top bar (<code>--dnf-topbar-height</code> + <code>--dnf-space-4</code>) while side by side</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-split--wide-aside</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>a 16-22rem side column that does not stick and stacks only below 64rem</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-container</code></td><td>block</td><td>full width up to <code>--dnf-content-max</code> (96rem), centred</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-container--narrow</code> / <code>--medium</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>at most 56rem / 80rem</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-divider</code></td><td>block</td><td>a 1px <code>--dnf-border</code> line, no margin</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-divider--vertical</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>1px wide, stretched (in a flex row)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-divider--label</code></td><td>modifier</td><td>text in the middle with a line on each side (<code>--dnf-subtle-foreground</code>, <code>text-sm</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-note</code></td><td>block</td><td>an icon and text in a row; <code>&gt; .dnf-icon</code> is one line high (<code>1lh</code>)</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-skip-link</code></td><td>block</td><td>a primary pill at the top start, moved out of view until <code>:focus</code></td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>dnf-js-only</code></td><td>utility</td><td>hidden until <code>dnf-theme.js</code> has marked <code>&lt;html class="dnf-js"&gt;</code> (before the first paint)</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>

<h2 id="api">API</h2>
<p>There are no tag helpers: the classes are the API. A typical screen:</p>
<ui-doc-code id="screen" lang="html">
<a class="dnf-skip-link" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
…
<main id="main" tabindex="-1">
    <div class="dnf-split">
        <div class="dnf-split__main">
            <div class="dnf-card">…</div>
        </div>
        <aside class="dnf-split__aside">
            <div class="dnf-card">…</div>
        </aside>
    </div>
</main>
</ui-doc-code>

<h2 id="accessibility">Accessibility</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Layout classes add no semantics: use landmarks (<code>&lt;main&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;aside&gt;</code>, <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code>)
        and headings in the markup.</li>
    <li>A labelled divider used as a separator gets <code>role="separator"</code>; a plain <code>&lt;hr&gt;</code> is one already.</li>
    <li>The skip link targets an element with an id and <code>tabindex="-1"</code>, so focus lands there.</li>
</ul>

<h2 id="guidelines">Guidelines</h2>
<ul>
    <li>Do use these classes for the recurring patterns and utilities for one-offs.</li>
    <li>Don't nest <code>dnf-container</code>s or put a fixed width on a grid child - let the grid size it.</li>
    <li>Don't rebuild a split or a grid with utilities on every screen - the primitives carry the breakpoints.</li>
</ul>
